---
import Icon from './Icon.astro';
---
<figure class="hero-film" data-hero data-film>
  <div class="film-frame">
    <video
      class="film-video"
      data-film-video
      controls
      muted
      loop
      playsinline
      preload="metadata"
      poster="/promo/concise-promo-poster.webp"
      width="1920"
      height="1080"
      aria-describedby="film-description"
    >
      <source src="/promo/concise-promo.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
    </video>
    <button class="film-start" type="button" data-film-start hidden>
      <span class="film-start-icon"><Icon name="play" size={22} /></span>
      Play the 31-second film
    </button>
    <div class="film-controls" data-film-controls hidden>
      <button type="button" class="film-control" data-film-sound aria-pressed="false">
        <span data-film-sound-off><Icon name="sound" size={18} /> Sound on</span>
        <span data-film-sound-on hidden><Icon name="muted" size={18} /> Mute</span>
      </button>
      <button type="button" class="film-control film-control-icon" data-film-pause aria-label="Pause film">
        <span data-film-pause-icon><Icon name="pause" size={18} /></span>
        <span data-film-play-icon hidden><Icon name="play" size={18} /></span>
      </button>
    </div>
  </div>
  {/* Screen readers only: the film's text, so nothing in it depends on seeing the video. */}
  <figcaption class="visually-hidden">
    <p id="film-description">A 31-second film: Concise checks it first. Stock agent phrases pile into a wall until an orange stroke cuts through it. Three checks follow, using real hook output on sample writes, then the web console.</p>
    <p>Comments: a four-line comment in <code>src/invoice.ts</code> is denied with <code>[concise] Comment at …/src/invoice.ts:1 is 4 lines (limit 2).</code> The example revision is <code>// Amounts are integer cents; never floats.</code></p>
    <p>Commit messages: AI-writing checks are optional and disabled by default. With them enabled, “Leverage a robust, seamless approach to streamline invoice rounding” is denied with <code>[concise] 3 AI writing patterns in commit message.</code> The example revision is “Round invoice totals to whole cents.”</p> <!-- taste-skill-ignore: quotes the input being checked -->
    <p>Pull requests: a three-paragraph PR body is denied with <code>[concise] PR/issue body is too verbose: 3 prose paragraphs (limit 1)</code>, shortened on screen. The example revision is “Rounds invoice totals to whole cents and updates the rounding tests.”</p>
    <p>The revisions show what the agent could write next. Concise does not rewrite files or commit messages.</p>
    <p>Real console screens follow: Live activity, Overview, Configuration, Playground, and Rules &amp; usage, under “Watch every check.” Start the console with <code>concise-web --all</code>.</p>
    <p>The film ends on “Your agent. Less verbose.”, the Concise mark, <code>/plugin install concise@be-concise</code>, and github.com/yannelli/be-concise.</p>
  </figcaption>
</figure>
